cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use the Scunthorpe Test, please cite it as below.
type: dataset
title: 'The Scunthorpe Test: a profanity-filter benchmark where blocking Scunthorpe counts against you'
abstract: >-
  A benchmark for profanity filters that reports how many innocent words a
  filter blocks beside how much profanity it catches: plain profanity, every
  disguise technique alone and combined (leetspeak, homoglyphs, spacing,
  zero-width characters), usernames, contextual cases, a Civil Comments
  sample of running text, and innocent words and phrases that contain a
  profane string, such as Scunthorpe. Each label is a function of the data.
  This repository carries the public dev split, the runner, adapters for
  open-source filters and the published results.
authors:
  - name: Unprofane
    website: https://unprofane.com
repository-code: https://github.com/unprofane/scunthorpe-test
url: https://unprofane.com/bench/scunthorpe/
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - profanity
  - profanity filter
  - content moderation
  - toxicity
  - false positives
  - Scunthorpe problem
  - benchmark
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-10-24'
